# Authors: Davide Batic and Dr. Denys Dutykh (Mathematics Department, Khalifa University
# of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE)
#
# Citation metadata in Citation File Format 1.2.0, from which GitHub draws its button
# "Cite this repository". The article that these codes accompany has been accepted for
# publication in Annals of Physics but has no published record yet, so the software itself
# is cited.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes, please cite this software as given below."
title: "tduality-bh: codes for the global and dynamical viability of the T-duality-inspired Bardeen regular black hole"
abstract: >-
  Python, Julia and Maple codes accompanying the article "Global and dynamical viability of
  the T-duality-inspired Bardeen regular black hole" by D. Batic and D. Dutykh, accepted for
  publication in Annals of Physics. The Python scripts draw the figures of the manuscript
  (geodesic potentials, radial diagnostics of the core, light rings, horizons and surface
  gravities, the filtered mass inflation, proper times) and check the closed form of a Bessel
  moment; the Maple worksheets and the Julia solver compute quasinormal modes of scalar and
  electromagnetic test fields by Chebyshev collocation in high precision.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: LGPL-2.1-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/dutykh/tduality-bh"
keywords:
  - bardeen-black-hole
  - black-holes
  - general-relativity
  - julia
  - maple
  - python
  - quasinormal-modes
  - regular-black-holes
  - reproducible-research
  - spectral-methods
  - t-duality
  - zero-point-length
